Z||000000||Cooter||04-30-2000||12:29 AM||||2 Questions about my 88GT:<BR>1.) Which temp sensor is the one that is in the front center of the intake manifold? I broke mine today while moving the engine around the garage floor.<BR>2.) Does the Fiero use a pilot shaft bushing? The crankshaft doesn't look like it has one in it and the pilot shaft has no wear on it where the bushing would be.<P>Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||mshill||04-30-2000||01:12 AM||||If it is sticking out horizontally, that is the ECM coolant temperature sensor. The radiator fan switch is sticking up vertically in the top front of the manifold.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||04-30-2000||07:29 AM||||Doesn't use pilot shaft bushing||||reg||1
